From 5c6777cf689946a8bab4d574fb0dd0c96a83202d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gillinger <christian.gillinger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:05:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] genesys: add support for the GL126 ASIC

The Genesys GL126 as its own command set. It is close enough to the
GL124 for the framework to fit, but its scan flow is the vendor's, so it
is a command set of its own rather than a GL124 model variant. The
register sequences are generated from USB captures of the vendor driver
and verified byte-exact against them; the generator is not part of this
series, its output (gl126_tables.cpp) is, with the provenance in the
header. gl126_lock.{h,cpp} keeps this backend and the reverse-engineered
companion driver off the one unit at once.
